  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "We have a perfectly clean world that even got featured from VRChat and praised by several VRChat devs on twitter, yet people managed to flag our world als \"environment-inappropriate\" simply by false-reporting it. There is absolutely nothing in our world that would deserve this flag.\nPeople can damage worlds with false reports and there is nothing that world creators can do against it. No counter-claim option, we are helpless.\nVRChat should never flag a world without checking if the report is valid and they should punish people for false reports. World creators need options to file a counter-report to initiate a check. Especially worlds with thousands of favorites need special treatment / protection.\nWe have creators who put hundreds of hours into a world, yet VRChat decides to trust a report from a random user more than their few creators? There should be a better balancing between this please.\n\nIntermediate solution could be to let the number of needed reports for a flag correlate with the number of visits and favorites on that world to avoid that a few reports damage a well-known world. Full solution would be to give creators an option to counter-claim reports.",
